{
 "sections": [
  {
   "blocks": [
    {
     "p": "Your party size is set by the outpost you leave from, and it stays with you through every portal you walk. A caravan is one long walk from a big outpost through smaller areas, vanquishing each with the bigger party: one instance, portal to portal, never stepping into an outpost."
    },
    {
     "p": "The times reckon about 4.5 foes a minute, walking included. A strong team with consumables manages about 7: one such run did the East caravan in about 6 hours."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "ToA East: Kryta, Shiverpeaks, Ascalon",
   "tab": "ToA East",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "p": "The long haul from {area:138}. Every area is entered once, except the two on the way to Dragon's Gullet, which are walked back through. Nothing can be bought on the way, so bring everything along: a Purveyor's Bell or Mercantile Summoning Stone for the drops, morale items or DP removers, res scrolls, lockpicks, consets, and Stalker's Rations and Bird's Eye Compasses to find the last foes and map as you go. It is a long time in one instance, though you can leave the game running and come back. If you'd rather not, or something breaks half way, the eastern half from {area:134} with 6 is a fair fallback: from Traveler's Vale on, the areas take only 4."
    },
